# BUSify — repository root ignore rules
# (frontend/.gitignore additionally covers node_modules/ and dist/)

# ─── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds JWT_SECRET, STUDENT_HASH_SALT, TRANSPORT_OFFICER_PASSWORD and
# ADMIN_PASSWORD. NEVER commit it. .env.example is the tracked template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ─── OSRM routing data (2-3 GB, regenerated by osrm-setup.sh) ───────────────
osrm_data/

# ─── Generated seed output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/seed/

# ─── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# ─── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ─── NOT ignored, on purpose ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# busify.db — backend/Dockerfile does `COPY busify.db ./data/busify.db`, so the
# build depends on it being present in the context. Shipping a binary database
# in the image is the wrong long-term design (it should be an Alembic migration
# plus a seed command); tracked as open item M-24 rather than silently breaking
# the Docker build.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
#
# busify.db holds student attendance rows keyed by HMAC-SHA256 hashes, not raw
# roll numbers, but it is still operational data. Review before any public push.